Infernux CPU JIT dependency distribution
======================================

This fork retains the llvmlite BSD-2-Clause license (LICENSE) and LLVM's
Apache-2.0 license with LLVM exception (LICENSE.thirdparty).

The Infernux wheel build repairs native shared-library dependencies. The
Windows LLVM 22.1.2 build currently includes:

  zlib 1.3.2 (zlib.dll): Jean-loup Gailly and Mark Adler; LICENSE.zlib.
  Zstandard 1.5.7 (zstd.dll): Meta Platforms, Inc. and affiliates;
    LICENSE.zstd (BSD-3-Clause option).
  Microsoft Visual C++ runtime (msvcp140.dll): Microsoft Corporation;
    LICENSE.windows-runtime. The validated Windows build uses 14.51.36247.

Repair tools may add a name suffix to private DLLs. That does not change
their authorship or license. These notices do not relicense any dependency
or grant additional redistribution rights. The Microsoft runtime is not
covered by the open-source licenses above. Redistribution is subject to the
applicable Visual Studio license and Microsoft's distributable-code list:

https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/windows/redistributing-visual-cpp-files
https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/visualstudio/releases/2022/redistribution

The supplied runtime license text is the convenience transcription included
with the runtime package; its own preamble describes its status. Windows
wheels include it; other platform wheels do not contain the Windows runtime.
Native dependency versions and licenses must be reviewed when changing the
build toolchain. A repaired wheel, not the raw build, is the release input.

Original projects:
  https://github.com/numba/llvmlite
  https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project
  https://zlib.net/
  https://facebook.github.io/zstd/
